# PetScape — project rules

The canonical instructions are in `AGENTS.md` at the repository root. Read it before working and
follow it; if any Cursor rule seems to conflict with it, `AGENTS.md` wins.

Non-negotiables (summary of AGENTS.md):

- Check the milestone **Status** in `docs/planning/milestones.md`; implement only the requested task
  from `docs/planning/task-breakdown.md`.
- Module boundaries: `PetScapeCore` is pure Swift (Foundation + `os` only). Platform and Rendering
  never import each other.
- No third-party dependencies, no private APIs, no singletons, no manipulation of other apps' windows.
- Original files under `assets/` are read-only.
- Run the relevant tests; never claim untested behavior works; do not commit unless asked.
- Update docs (and ADRs for architectural changes) together with code.
